WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.381 --> 00:00:16.172
The was back on in our apartment building.

2
00:00:17.353 --> 00:00:17.814
But Mr.

3
00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:21.336
Calabria said no one could turn on any air conditioners yet.

4
00:00:22.858 --> 00:00:25.620
The workmen needed to put in special wiring for that.

5
00:00:27.001 --> 00:00:30.564
But our lights were back on, and our refrigerator was humming again.

6
00:00:32.116 --> 00:00:33.297
My head was humming too.

7
00:00:37.361 --> 00:00:39.543
have a plan," I told my friends.

8
00:00:39.563 --> 00:00:42.045
"Let's teach Tufty to talk.

9
00:00:43.346 --> 00:00:46.809
Then maybe he'll talk instead of making loud noises."

10
00:00:46.829 --> 00:00:50.433
"But, Iggy," Jenny reminded me.

11
00:00:50.453 --> 00:00:52.615
"Tufty doesn't talk.

12
00:00:53.596 --> 00:00:55.898
I don't think he can learn to say any words."

13
00:00:57.039 --> 00:00:58.220
I thought for a moment.

14
00:00:59.948 --> 00:01:03.771
"I did a research project in school about parrots," I said.

15
00:01:03.791 --> 00:01:10.136
"You can teach them to talk by repeating the same words over and over again."

16
00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:15.360
Josh seemed to like my idea.

17
00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:19.404
"We could use my computer to make a recording," he said.

18
00:01:19.424 --> 00:01:22.906
"Then we could play it over and over for Tufty."

19
00:01:22.926 --> 00:01:25.449
"That's a great idea!"

20
00:01:25.829 --> 00:01:26.309
I said.

21
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.512
Josh ran downstairs to get his computer.

22
00:01:31.272 --> 00:01:36.934
"Since Molly is Tufty's owner, I think she should make the recording," I suggested.

23
00:01:36.954 --> 00:01:40.335
A few minutes later, Josh came back.

24
00:01:41.395 --> 00:01:44.356
He plugged in his computer and placed it in front of Molly.

25
00:01:44.376 --> 00:01:47.236
"Ready?" asked Josh.

26
00:01:47.256 --> 00:01:49.837
"Wait!" cried Molly.

27
00:01:50.317 --> 00:01:51.898
"What am I supposed to say?"

28
00:01:51.918 --> 00:02:00.280
"Say something calming," Jenny suggested, "like 'Now it's time to go to sleep.'"

29
00:02:01.792 --> 00:02:05.375
"But Tufty is already asleep," I pointed out.

30
00:02:06.535 --> 00:02:10.738
Sure enough, Tufty was still asleep with his head under his wing.

31
00:02:12.279 --> 00:02:14.301
"I'll wake him up," said Molly.

32
00:02:14.321 --> 00:02:18.343
"Tufty!" she said, gently nudging him.

33
00:02:18.824 --> 00:02:19.484
"Wake up!"

34
00:02:22.766 --> 00:02:26.949
Tufty woke up and opened his mouth wide.

35
00:02:26.969 --> 00:02:30.952
"Uh-oh, here comes the subway train!"

36
00:02:31.432 --> 00:02:32.353
cried Jenny.

37
00:02:33.474 --> 00:02:35.395
Everyone put their hands over their ears.

38
00:02:36.596 --> 00:02:38.498
But all Tufty did was yawn.

39
00:02:42.281 --> 00:02:44.523
at least he's awake now," said Josh.

40
00:02:45.844 --> 00:02:49.807
Josh tapped a key on his computer, and Molly started recording.

41
00:02:49.827 --> 00:02:57.534
"My name is Tufty, and I'm a very quiet parrot," she said softly.

42
00:02:57.554 --> 00:02:59.956
"Good!" said Josh.

43
00:03:01.384 --> 00:03:05.305
"Now I'll fix the computer so Molly's recording will repeat over and over."

44
00:03:07.326 --> 00:03:09.746
Josh pressed more buttons on his computer.

45
00:03:10.847 --> 00:03:13.527
Then he pressed a key to play Molly's recording.

46
00:03:13.547 --> 00:03:21.510
"My name is Tufty, and I'm a very quiet parrot," we heard Molly say.

47
00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:25.891
Tufty opened his eyes and cocked his head.

48
00:03:25.911 --> 00:03:26.811
"He's listening!"

49
00:03:27.451 --> 00:03:28.431
whispered Jenny.

50
00:03:31.745 --> 00:03:36.329
"Let's leave him alone so he can pay attention," I said.

51
00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:39.792
We went in Molly's room and played cards.

52
00:03:41.113 --> 00:03:48.299
From the living room, we could hear Molly's voice again and again: "My name is Tufty, and I'm

53
00:03:48.399 --> 00:03:50.601
a very quiet parrot."

54
00:03:52.082 --> 00:03:53.583
Molly glanced at a clock.

55
00:03:53.603 --> 00:03:58.107
"How long do you think it will take for Tufty to learn to talk?"

56
00:03:58.627 --> 00:03:59.208
she asked.

57
00:04:00.408 --> 00:04:02.729
"We'll go back in twenty minutes," I said.

58
00:04:02.749 --> 00:04:04.810
"That should be long enough.

59
00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.131
Parrots are smart."

60
00:04:07.171 --> 00:04:11.153
Exactly twenty minutes later, we all crept back into the living room.

61
00:04:12.633 --> 00:04:15.895
Molly's voice was still droning away on the computer.

62
00:04:17.555 --> 00:04:19.896
But Tufty was fast asleep!

63
00:04:19.916 --> 00:04:24.298
"I guess my voice put him back to sleep," said Molly.

64
00:04:24.318 --> 00:04:26.679
"He didn't learn a thing!"

65
00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:28.020
groaned Jenny.

66
00:04:29.132 --> 00:04:31.154
"Don't be so sure," I said.

67
00:04:31.174 --> 00:04:34.937
"Sometimes people learn new things in their sleep.

68
00:04:35.558 --> 00:04:36.979
Maybe parrots can too."

69
00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:40.402
At that moment Tufty opened his eyes.

70
00:04:41.463 --> 00:04:42.423
He shook his feathers.

71
00:04:43.304 --> 00:04:46.287
Then he stood on one foot and opened his beak.

72
00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.429
"Look! He's going to talk!"

73
00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:50.690
cried Molly.

74
00:04:51.571 --> 00:04:52.832
But Tufty didn't talk.

75
00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:55.475
Instead he made a sound.

76
00:05:00.408 --> 00:05:05.651
Broo-ooo-oot! It was the longest, loudest car horn I had ever heard.

77
00:05:06.952 --> 00:05:08.633
Molly's mom ran into the room.

78
00:05:08.653 --> 00:05:11.455
"Molly!" she cried.

79
00:05:11.475 --> 00:05:13.236
"Tufty is too loud!

80
00:05:13.596 --> 00:05:15.297
He has to quiet down by tonight.

81
00:05:16.478 --> 00:05:19.400
If he doesn't, we'll have to find him a new home!"
